Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(client): add spools and print their labels in one
 step
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The add-spool dialog already creates N spools from its count field. This adds
a second submit button that then prints a label for each one, for the case
this is really for: four rolls of the same filament arrive, you type 4, and
you want four labels without visiting the label page afterwards.

Creation and printing stay separate. The spools are created through the
existing path, and printing runs strictly after it and cannot throw, so a
printer that is off or unplugged never costs you the spools you just entered
— it only changes the message you get.

The button is shown only when a printer is configured and a spool label
design exists, so the dialog is unchanged for everyone else.
